# API Conventions

## Responses

Use `App\Http\Controllers\Api\BaseController`:

- Success: `{ success: true, message, data }`
- Error: `{ success: false, message, errors? }`
- Prefer API Resources for model payloads.
- Never trust client-sent prices/totals — recalculate on the server.

## Controllers

- Thin: authorize → call service → return resource.
- Type-hint FormRequests for validation.
- Protect cart/order/checkout with `auth:sanctum`.
- Products listing/details are public unless specified otherwise.

## Validation & HTTP status

| Case | Status |
|------|--------|
| Validation failed | 422 |
| Unauthenticated | 401 |
| Forbidden | 403 |
| Not found | 404 |
| Insufficient stock / business rule | 422 or 409 |
| Conflict (concurrency) | 409 |

Meaningful messages for: product not found, insufficient stock, invalid/expired coupon, usage limit, empty cart, invalid order status, unauthorized order access.

## Routes

- Module routes in `Modules/*/routes/api.php` (already prefixed with `api`).
- Prefer explicit routes over fat `apiResource` when only a subset is needed.
- Keep URL shapes aligned with Requirements (`/products`, `/cart/items`, `/checkout`, `/orders`).
